Package: kwbackup
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: rclone
Suggests: default-mysql-client | mariadb-client, postgresql-client, zstd | gzip, pigz, rar
Description: backup tool for databases, file storage and archives
 kwbackup dumps databases, syncs directories and packs file archives, then
 uploads the result to any rclone remote (S3, WebDAV, SFTP, ...).
 .
 Three scenarios: mysqldump/mariadb-dump/pg_dump/sqlite3 piped through
 zstd/gzip/rar, rclone sync or copy of local directories, and tar archives
 with include/exclude patterns.
 .
 Retention is counted per class (daily, weekly, monthly), either as a number
 of copies to keep or as an age window. The command line can list and verify
 what is really stored, and restore a database, an archive or a storage tree.
